To keep him up to date with the happenings at home, Jane would send her father handwritten letters detailing the little events of her day, which Jim would keep tucked safely in his briefcase to read each night for a reminder of home. One such letter read, But Aunty, Mummy and I swam in the three-foot six-inch pool. While we were there, I learnt how to open my eyes under the water forever so long, and I learnt how to kick my legs and make my arms float. And dive, gracefully dive, races dive and plane dive. I learnt all this from Aunty Tali. There is only one thing I can't do, breathing out as I'm swimming along. Tonight, I had a hot pie, fritz and sauce sandwich, and rainbow ice cream. Aunty Tali bought a great big roast chicken from her father for nothing. Most of all, I want to wish you much luck with your hot, tiring work.
为了让他了解家里的最新情况，简会给父亲写手写信，详细描述她白天的琐事，吉姆会把这些信安全地夹在公文包里，每天晚上阅读，以此作为对家的回忆。其中一封信写道：“但是阿姨，妈咪和我在那个三英尺六英寸深的游泳池里游泳了。在我们去的那段时间里，我学会了如何在水里睁开眼睛好久好久，我还学会了如何踢腿、让胳膊浮起来。还有跳水，优雅地跳水，赛跑跳水和平板跳水。这一切都是我从塔利阿姨那里学来的。只有一件事我不会，那就是一边游泳一边呼气。今晚，我吃了一个热派、弗里茨和酱汁三明治以及彩虹冰淇淋。塔利阿姨白白从她父亲那里买了一只非常大的烤鸡。最重要的是，我祝你辛苦又劳累的工作一切顺利。”

